WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:06.000
Mr. Josh Rigmaiden would go and say, "I got a young man here in Mossville.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.340
He need a job because he got a family.

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.180
He got four kids.

4
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:17.940
Y'all try to help him." [1:09:31] So eventually . . . And the old saying, “You scratch my back I'll scratch yours.”

5
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:26.620
But a lot of people won't admit a lot of things happened simply because of leadership that you followed.

6
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:35.340
When politicians saw that you were on one accord, that was power.

7
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.540
You had power when you were all together.

8
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.660
And they used to tell us if we stick together . . . They used to demonstrate.

9
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.820
I'm serious.

10
00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.920
If you were a kid here, a young man or woman or whoever from this community,

11
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.100
and something happened . . . if you got in a wreck,

12
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.300
got in a brawl, or got whatever, got into trouble that they had to say,

13
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:01.600
"We going to arrest you and bring you to jail," you called Josh Rigmaiden.

14
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.320
Josh Rigmaiden would call Ham Reed and say, "That's one of my boys.

15
00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:08.360
Don't you lock him up no further than where he's at.

16
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.260
I'll be there to get him."

17
00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.580
That was a done deal.

18
00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.740
Who's Ham Reed?

19
00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.880
He used to be the . . . That's right, you not from here.

20
00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.340
Ham Reed was the sheriff of Calcasieu Parish for years.

21
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:30.880
And Mr. Frank Salter was at that time back in the day was the . . . What was Frank Salter?

22
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.640
District attorney.

23
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.740
But people respected Josh Rigmaiden.

24
00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.800
And they saw a community that was together.

25
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.380
Simple as that.

26
00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.920
And everybody went.

27
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:44.880
They would talk it over.

28
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.180
Who's going to be your next sheriff?

29
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.660
Who's going to be the district attorney?

30
00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:56.760
And at that time you had, in the parish, if you had extra 2,000 votes, that was a lot for you.

31
00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.300
Five hundred votes, man I want those five hundred votes.

32
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.300
Yep.

33
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:06.660
So that's the way I can remember things for the community.

34
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.960
Voting is power.

35
00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.260
Voting is power.

36
00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:15.180
So Josh Rigmaiden, what made him so effective?

37
00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.700
What made him so effective?

38
00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.380
Unity.

39
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.060
And his ability to get everybody . . .?

40
00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:24.640
His ability to get everybody together and the unity.

41
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:34.920
And I don't know, I'm just saying they didn't fear him, but he was a man that had the right words.

42
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.300
He had a way of having people to follow him.

43
00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.580
He was business.

44
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:44.020
He had a little business, a little store and this, that and the other.

45
00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:49.080
Mr. Josh was, to us, a powerful man.

46
00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:56.700
A lot of things happened with unions . . . changeover in government.

47
00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:06.320
So this made Mossville not as effective as they were in the '40s and '50s . . . or in the '50s,

48
00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:17.420
so somewhere in the early '60s it began to change because of government change was one thing.

49
00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.120
But some things you can’t get from being radical.

50
00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.900
I'm going to use that word.

51
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:34.400
You had more people that wanted to just take things over in a radical way than a way of words and wisdom and understanding.

52
00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.420
Like a gentle . . .

53
00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.220
A gentleness.

54
00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.460
Even the Bible speak that a soft answer turns away wrath.
